## Complex rule assistant drafts removal (DELETE) rules

### Context
Asking the Complex rule assistant "remove the meters owned when a contract is terminated"
produced no usable rule: its prompt allowed only SPARQL CONSTRUCT and forbade DELETE, its
`update_draft` tool had no notion of rule kind, and the editor hid the assistant for removal
rules. The engine and editor already support removal rules (`kind: removal`). This is a material
change to an LLM agent, so it follows the AI-feature gate (`.cursor/12-ai-feature-lifecycle.mdc`):
local SPEC (`.planning/complex-rule-builder-removal/SPEC.md`), a committed eval dataset, a
baseline MLflow run on the unchanged agent, the change, and a second run.
Decision (user): when a removal request does not say what should disappear, the assistant asks
(only the link, the entity itself, or only its class membership).

### Changes
1. `src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/engine.py`:
   - System prompt covers both kinds (construct / removal), the accepted removal forms
     (`DELETE {…} WHERE {…}`, `DELETE WHERE`, `DELETE DATA`) and limits (no INSERT, GRAPH,
     OPTIONAL, property paths, variable predicates), the guard (a constant or class scope;
     never a whole-predicate or whole-graph delete), the "what disappears" question asked first,
     the entity-removal rule (class membership + the link the condition uses, no extra required
     patterns), and a Preview reminder.
   - The draft snapshot and the system prompt carry the rule `kind`.
   - `_reply_text`: when the model ends a turn with an empty message after `propose_options`,
     the reply is the options' question instead of "I couldn't display that answer".
   - Removed an unused `Callable` import.
2. `src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/tools.py`: `RULE_KIND_CONSTRUCT` / `RULE_KIND_REMOVAL`;
   `update_draft` takes `kind` (enum in the schema), rejects an unknown kind, and stores it on the
   draft.
3. `src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py`: assistant route docstring documents `kind` in
   `current_draft` and `draft`.
4. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js`: the draft sent to the assistant
   carries the Rule type; `_craApplyDraftKind` applies the kind of the assistant's draft (shows the
   Preview box for a removal); the assistant stays available for removal rules (the "written by
   hand" layout is gone) and changing the Rule type keeps the conversation; new greeting.
5. `src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-business-rules.css`: removed the `cra-layout--manual`
   rules. `src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html`: removal hint no
   longer says removals are written by hand.
6. Eval harness (new):
   - `tests/eval/datasets/agent_complex_rule_builder/baseline.jsonl` — 15 rows: CONSTRUCT
     regressions, link / membership / attribute / class-scoped removals, three answers to the
     "what disappears" question, the two real ambiguous requests from the 2026-11-26 log, and
     adversarial requests (wipe the graph, INSERT + DELETE in one rule).
   - `tests/eval/judges/complex_rule_builder.py` — rule-based judges: kind, query compiles with
     `SPARQLRuleEngine.validate_rule`, intent terms, clarification, safety.
   - `tests/eval/run_agent_complex_rule_builder.py` — dry run (dataset contract) and live run
     (calls the agent, logs to MLflow `/Shared/ontobricks/agents/complex_rule_builder`); refuses to
     score or log LLM transport failures.
   - `tests/eval/thresholds.yaml` — `complex_rule_builder` (aggregate 0.80);
     `tests/eval/README.md` status row.
7. Tests: `tests/units/agents/test_agent_complex_rule_builder.py` (draft kind, unknown kind,
   schema, kind in the prompt, empty-reply fallback, removal prompt content);
   `tests/units/front/test_business_rules_removal_ui.py` (assistant kept for removals, draft kind
   applied); `tests/eval/test_run_agent_complex_rule_builder.py` (new, 12 offline tests: dataset
   contract, judges, live wiring, transport-failure abort).
8. `docs/user-guide.md`: Removal Rules section describes the assistant drafting removals.

