## Complex rule assistant: the question behind the answer buttons is always shown

### Context
Asking "Remove the meters owned when a contract is terminated" showed answer buttons
(`Contract :hasMeter Meter` / `Customer :owns Meter` / Both) under the reply "I'll wait for
your answers to both questions above", but no question was visible. Three causes: the editor
rendered only the buttons of `options`, never `options.question`; a second `propose_options`
call in one turn silently replaced the first question; and `describe_class` listed only
outgoing relationships, so the model could not see that both `hasMeter` and `owns` point to
Meter and either asked inconsistently or picked `hasMeter` silently.

### Changes
1. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js` — new `_craReplyWithQuestion(data)`:
   when the reply does not contain the options' question, the question is appended. Used for
   the chat bubble and for the history sent back on the next turn, so the model also knows
   what it asked.
2. `src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/tools.py` — `propose_options` refuses a second call
   in the same turn (keeps the first question, tells the model to ask one question at a time)
   and refuses a single-answer question. `describe_class` now also returns
   `incomingProperties` (relationships whose range is the class, with their domain).
3. `src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/engine.py` — prompt: one question per turn, written
   in the reply, never "questions above"; no single-option questions; use the literal the
   user gave; new "Which link" rule (call `describe_class` on the removed entity's class and
   ask which relationship when more than one could fit).
4. Eval harness — `tests/eval/run_agent_complex_rule_builder.py` records the tools called per
   turn and takes `--dataset baseline|regression|all`; `judge_clarifies` scores 0 when a turn
   calls `propose_options` more than once or offers buttons without question text; new
   `meter_contract_owns` fixture; `"entities"` accepted as the entity choice.
5. `tests/eval/datasets/agent_complex_rule_builder/regression.jsonl` (new) — 3 rows from the
   reported flow: first question, which link after "Only the link", the `owns` removal draft.
6. Tests — tool refusals, `incomingProperties`, prompt rules
   (`tests/units/agents/test_agent_complex_rule_builder.py`); question display under node
   (`tests/units/front/test_complex_rule_assistant_question.py`, new); judge and runner
   (`tests/eval/test_run_agent_complex_rule_builder.py`).
7. `docs/user-guide.md` — the assistant asks which link, one question at a time, with the
   question above its buttons. `tests/eval/README.md` — dataset row count.

### Eval (endpoint benoit_cayla.ontobricks_dev_repository.bcay_ai_gateway)
