## docs: contributors list, third-party licenses refresh, release-notes routine

### Context
The release-notes routine did not cover the contributors list or the third-party licenses.
CONTRIBUTORS.md was missing several GitHub contributors, and licenses/README.md had drifted
from the dependencies declared in pyproject.toml (stale versions, LGPL psycopg presented as
permissive). Same change as the 0.9.4 branch.

### Changes
1. `CONTRIBUTORS.md` - added Alex Picard (Core Team) and the missing community contributors
   with merged PRs: LaurentPRAT-DB, arunnayar-byte, Amine Kerboute (CactusQuill), Diego Antonelli.
2. `.cursorrules` - the "Release Notes" routine now also updates CONTRIBUTORS.md (GitHub
   contributors + merged PR authors) and checks/updates /licenses/ against the current
   dependencies.
3. `licenses/README.md` - APScheduler `>=3.10,<4`; databricks-sql-connector `>=4.7.0` with the
   `[kernel]` extra (databricks-sql-kernel, Apache-2.0); DOMPurify license expression; neo4j
   note; new "Lakebase Registry" section with the psycopg LGPL-3.0 notice (used unmodified as
   an external library); updated License Summary and closing sentence. The license files
   under `licenses/` were already present on this branch and are unchanged.

