## fix(reasoning): forward-port #239 - OWL axioms drive scalable graph reasoning (#237)

Context: Forward-port of PR #239 (merged on `0.9.4`, squash commit 37f00273) to
`0.10.0`. OWL axioms declared in Expr. & Axioms never produced instance-level
inferences; `run_graph_reasoning` only used the legacy property-characteristics
panel whose save routes were removed.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py - `run_graph_reasoning` also reads
   `ontology["axioms"]`: a self `owl:propertyChainAxiom` of exactly two elements
   (`p ∘ p ⊑ p`) marks `p` transitive and runs the scalable SQL
   `transitive_closure(p)`. New helpers `_find_transitive_from_axioms` and
   `_resolve_axiom_prop_uri`.
2. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py - `propertyChain` falls back to
   `subject` when `resultProperty` is absent (the UI stores `subject`), so
   UI-created chains are exported to OWL; a null chain no longer raises.
3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-axioms.js - the result property is
   required for `propertyChain`; label reads "Result Property".
4. tests/units/ontology/test_reasoning_service.py,
   tests/units/ontology/test_owl_generator.py - coverage for self-chain
   detection, 3-element/mixed/imported/null-chain cases and UI-shape export.

Not in this change (follow-up on #237): `owl:inverseOf` SQL expansion and
general `p ∘ q ⊑ r` chains.

